"""Calendar-record checks for Thunderbird tasks with a local profile.

A Thunderbird calendar task ends with event records stored in the profile's
``calendar-data/local.sqlite`` database.  This module snapshots that database
(together with its ``-wal`` and ``-shm`` siblings) into a temporary directory,
reads the copy read-only, and joins ``cal_events`` against ``cal_properties``
(LOCATION / DESCRIPTION / CATEGORIES), ``cal_alarms`` and ``cal_recurrence``.

Event times are stored as microsecond epochs and are restored to wall-clock
time with each event's own ``event_start_tz`` / ``event_end_tz`` through
:mod:`zoneinfo`.  The declared titles, counts, times, durations, recurrences
and alarms are then compared exactly.

A missing profile, a missing calendar database, or an unreadable database is
reported as a plain failure: the calendar records the task asks for have not
been produced.
"""

